From 0c8ab7cfa8c6bd5a36a6aa14284482c83c68fc44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: squadron_process <noreply@p0g-stack>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Worker: pluggable channel factory

Worker.start() always opens Channel.open(), so a worker can only run in
an isolate (VM) or a Web Worker (browser). Channel is already an
interface, but the worker's channel is private, so a custom Channel has
no way in.

Add a ChannelFactory typedef and Worker.channelFactory (constructor
parameter and settable field). When set, start() awaits the factory
instead of Channel.open(); everything after it (stats, the shared
_openChannel future, stop()) is unchanged. With no factory, behavior is
identical to before.

Export SquadronCancelationToken and StreamId, which a Channel
implementation needs for cancelToken() and cancelStream().

Tests: test/13_channel_factory_suite.dart, run by both the VM and
browser runners (wrapping Channel.open, replacing the channel, one open
for concurrent first requests, factory errors reaching the caller, the
default path).
